      "updated": 1773032605476,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Joins\n    1. CROSS JOIN - This join is basically used when there is no column having same name in the joining tables otherwise it becomes\ninner join.\n\n    2. INNER JOIN\n        Note: You cannot just write the name of the column even though the name is same in both the tables. -> Error Code: 1052.\nColumn 'id' in on clause is ambiguous.\n        But in self join you can write just the column name since only one table is used for joining.\n        \n    → In lot of LeetCode questions, The joining is something like T1.clo1 <= T2.col2\n\n    3. RIGHT / LEFT JOIN - The values corrosponding to the records from right table which is not involved in the group by there\nvalues for the features of the left table considered as NULL.\n\n    4. FULL OUTER JOIN - using `UNION`\n    5. SELF JOIN\n    \n    → Joining over more than one column: ON T1.col1 = T2.col1 AND T1.col2 <= T2.col2\n\n    6. Set Operations:\n        1. UNION\n        2. UNION ALL\n        3. INTERSECT\n        4. EXCEPT\n\n    → `JOIN` without JOIN statment - In below SQL query each id from T1 will be compared with each id in T2 and for each\n`true` result it will return the id in the table.",
      "fontSize": 16.06983696858507,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Joins\n    1. CROSS JOIN - This join is basically used when there is no column having same name in the joining tables otherwise it becomes inner join.\n\n    2. INNER JOIN\n        Note: You cannot just write the name of the column even though the name is same in both the tables. -> Error Code: 1052. Column 'id' in on clause is ambiguous.\n        But in self join you can write just the column name since only one table is used for joining.\n        \n    → In lot of LeetCode questions, The joining is something like T1.clo1 <= T2.col2\n\n    3. RIGHT / LEFT JOIN - The values corrosponding to the records from right table which is not involved in the group by there values for the features of the left table considered as NULL.\n\n    4. FULL OUTER JOIN - using `UNION`\n    5. SELF JOIN\n    \n    → Joining over more than one column: ON T1.col1 = T2.col1 AND T1.col2 <= T2.col2\n\n    6. Set Operations:\n        1. UNION\n        2. UNION ALL\n        3. INTERSECT\n        4. EXCEPT\n\n    → `JOIN` without JOIN statment - In below SQL query each id from T1 will be compared with each id in T2 and for each `true` result it will return the id in the table.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
